WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:03.461 line:0%
<i>Last night's State of the Union
was an irrefutable disaster.</i>

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.463
Is the President going
to drop out of the race?

00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:08.007 align:end position:100%
<i>Congress truly is in a sorry, sorry state.</i>

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.592 align:end position:100% line:0%
<i>The system is broken!</i>

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.969 align:end position:100% line:0%
<i>And you people broke it!</i>

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:13.221 align:end position:100%
Well, I really screwed that up, didn't I?

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:18.643
<i>Each one of you has been with
me from the beginning of this ride.</i>

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.854 align:end position:100%
<i>So, I need your opinion.</i>

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:22.772 align:end position:100%
If you run and if you lose...

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.940 align:end position:100%
that's your legacy.

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.525 align:end position:100%
I think you're asking the wrong thing.

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:27.652 position:59%
The question should be:
"Why am I running in the first place?"

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:34.200 position:63%
<i>Our President is not embracing all of us
as American citizens.</i>

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:36.161 position:63%
<i>I don't feel like anybody represents me.</i>

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.164
You're concerned about making
the wrong decisions.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:41.249
<i>Any leader worth a damn would be.</i>

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:43.126
It makes sense to be angry.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.544
Angry like all of you are!

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:45.628
Hell, I am with you!

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:47.797 position:66%
<i>Keep showing the voters who you really are</i>

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.132 position:59%
and the rest will take care of itself.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.595 position:61%
Think about whether you'd like to join
the ticket as Kirkman's Vice President.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.307 position:56%
Why would you keep this to yourself?

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.391
What the hell were you thinking?

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:00.393
<i>Whatever happened to standards?</i>

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:02.145
What happened to ethical practices?

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:05.315 position:58%
So, everyone has the right to privacy
except when it's convenient for you?

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:08.109
This isn't journalism!

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:09.277
Why aren't you mad?

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.403
I know the truth.

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:15.241
How would you like to come
work for the C.I.A.?

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:17.285 position:56%
<i>There's been an outbreak in Toronto.</i>

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:18.953
We need to make contact before
an unfriendly does.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.080 position:66%
We have to be prepared for the possibility

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:22.582
of a vile terrorist attack.

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:26.377
What's your call, Mr. President?

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:27.879
I am guessing here.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:29.631 position:59%
You may not have what it takes to win.

00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:31.674 position:59%
Because what it takes is ruthlessness.

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:34.844
You want me to march around
the White House

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.137
picking fights with the President?

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:37.096
You're a coward.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.350
You took away my right to choose.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.393
I'm sorry that I lied.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:43.770
Lynn?

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:45.146
I need an ambulance right away.

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:47.524
Oh, my God.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.240 position:61%
I've gone all in for what I think
is right for the heart of this country.

00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:57.158
<i>You hold yourself above politics!</i>

00:01:57.408 --> 00:02:00.203
The truth is, you're every bit
as much a politician as I am.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:02.205
God help me if that's true.

